From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GKI KernelSU SUSFS <root>
Date: Mon Jan  1 00:00:00 2026 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: skip blocktag hook for synchronous fuse requests

MTK's blocktag vendor hook (BTMTR) emits block_io_start and
block_io_get_result trace calls while holding fiq->lock. When the
vendor's io-called hook needs a synchronous FUSE request (e.g. after
statfs()/getattr()), this deadlocks: the tracing triggers a sync
request which competes for fiq->lock (or hangs the requesting thread),
manifesting as a hang, watchdog reset, or SoftLockup right after boot
once userspace performs statfs() checks.

Keep the vendor hook for asynchronous (background) requests only:
reads/writes/background writeback. The crash-triggering synchronous
userspace calls (statfs/getattr/lookup/fsync) now bypass the hook.

Signed-off-by: GKI KernelSU SUSFS <root>
diff --git a/fs/fuse/dev.c b/fs/fuse/dev.c
index d0bf4bc..ebfc006 100644
--- a/fs/fuse/dev.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/dev.c
@@ -236,6 +236,14 @@ __releases(fiq->lock)
 		fuse_len_args(req->args->in_numargs,
 			      (struct fuse_arg *) req->args->in_args);
 	list_add_tail(&req->list, &fiq->pending);
+	/*
+	 * MTK blocktag's block_io_start/block_io_get_result trace calls
+	 * are not safe to run while holding fiq->lock, and on some devices
+	 * they trigger a synchronous request (and thus a deadlock, a hang,
+	 * or a watchdog reset) right after statfs(). Keep the vendor hook,
+	 * but only invoke it for asynchronous (background) requests.
+	 */
+	if (!sync)
 	trace_android_vh_queue_request_and_unlock(&fiq->waitq, sync);
 	fiq->ops->wake_pending_and_unlock(fiq, sync);
 }
